## Scope and counting rule

The current delivery uses each report's original **meta.intakeTag**, as requested by the human. Deduplicate by report id, then group the reports merged into #4471 by that unchanged label. Do not use causeOf to determine membership for this delivery. Original labels and computed causes are different sources of classification, not interchangeable diagnoses.

The earlier three-ticket split has been superseded. Issue #3 is closed; its five reports are counted once, under their original parser label in #1. No source report or original tenant configuration has been edited.

<IncidentEvidence />

## Two active tickets

### Parser-tagged reports

[Issue #1](https://github.com/ldomzalski-allegro/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/1) contains all reports originally labelled parser. A typical described problem is a day/month date being interpreted month/day: R-41200 says 7 April became 4 July. Its proposed remedy is locale-consistent parsing or an unambiguous date representation, with regression coverage for ambiguous dates, invalid dates and relevant entry paths.

Membership follows the intake label, not an independent diagnosis. Some parser-tagged reports compute to hint in the exported model. The five desk-noted descriptions remain visible as diagnostic caveats: one-day shifts, different days in Lisbon and Toronto, and an invite said to arrive before booking. Their wording does not establish a common timezone or other third cause. A label alone does not prove that one parser fix will resolve every report.

### Hint-tagged reports

[Issue #2](https://github.com/ldomzalski-allegro/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/2) contains all reports originally labelled hint. The supplied code describes booking-v3 printing MM/DD/YYYY for day-first tenants while the form reads the tenant's date convention. Correct the hint and verify that the input example, accepted format and saved date agree.

This original-label bucket is not limited to booking-v3 form reports: some hint-tagged reports compute to parser. Do not present every report in this ticket as a confirmed form-hint failure. Verify tenant locale, form, channel and reproduction evidence before implementing a fix.

## Original computed-cause view: comparison, not ticket membership

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

The original component is preserved. Its totals are the results of causeOf, not the original intakeTag counts used by the current issues. Its “no ticket of its own” text refers to the original desk snapshot, not the current GitHub issues. This discrepancy is explicitly disclosed rather than changing the export to force agreement.

## Why subject matching is insufficient

This proposed record does not rewrite accepted [decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject). That record and the [triage page](/kb/triage/dedupe) merge on subject alone. The examples below show that identical subjects can have different modeled causes and different subjects can share a cause. Subject-only matching is not evidence of the same technical problem.

<DedupeExplorer />

For future triage, read the body and verify the entry path and tenant context. Keep the original intake label for provenance, but do not treat it as a verified cause. Record discrepancies and establish causes before merging unrelated reports or claiming a fix covers them. The current two-bucket publication tests the human-requested original-label grouping; it does not settle those discrepancies.

## Received is not merged

<QueueTimeline ticket={4471} />

A batch of merges is not the start of an incident. Receipt dates begin in April and the snapshot ends on 4 October 2026; it does not prove reporting stopped afterwards. The desk covers multiple products. Do not infer a failure rate from the stated sched-prod population or assign every report to that product without evidence.

## Review and limitations

Support should review new reports and classification discrepancies; engineering should reproduce each mechanism and add targeted regression tests. This export contains no live queue, booking-service implementation or event trace sufficient to reproduce every unusual description. Neither a queued fix nor this page proves a product fix shipped. Recompute from a new snapshot before relying on these counts as current.

